            "id": "13998441",
            "headline": "Blackstone-owned AGS Health files updated DRHP for Rs 4,800 crore India IPO",
            "heading": "Blackstone-owned AGS Health files updated DRHP for Rs 4,800 crore India IPO",
            "intro": "AGS Health IPO | The company plans to raise Rs 1,800 crore through a fresh issue of shares, while BCP Asia II Topco VIII Pte, an investment holding company owned by The Blackstone Group, will offload shares worth Rs 3,000 crore through an offer for sale.",
            "body": "Blackstone Group-owned AGS Health, a revenue cycle management (RCM) solutions provider for US healthcare providers, has filed its updated draft red herring prospectus (DRHP) with the Securities and Exchange Board of India (SEBI) on August 7 to raise up to Rs 4,800 crore through an initial public offering (IPO).\r\n\r\nThe company plans to raise Rs 1,800 crore through a fresh issue of shares, while BCP Asia II Topco VIII Pte, an investment holding company owned by The Blackstone Group, will offload shares worth Rs 3,000 crore through an offer for sale (OFS).\r\n\r\nAs part of the fresh issue, AGS Health may also undertake a pre-IPO placement of up to Rs 360 crore. If the company proceeds with the pre-IPO placement, the amount raised will be deducted from the size of the fresh issue.\r\n\r\nAGS Health had filed its IPO papers through the confidential route with the capital markets regulator during March-April 2026. Subsequently, SEBI approved the draft papers in June 2026.\r\n\r\nThe Tamil Nadu-based company intends to utilise Rs 1,600 crore from the net proceeds of the fresh issue to repay debt of its indirect subsidiaries\u2014AGS Health BCP LLC and AGS Health BCP Holdings, Inc. As of March 2026, the company had consolidated outstanding borrowings of Rs 4,238.8 crore.\r\n\r\nThe remaining proceeds from the fresh issue will be used for general corporate purposes, while the proceeds from the offer for sale will accrue to BCP Asia II Topco.\r\n\r\nClick Here Read All IPO News\r\n\r\nAGS Health contracts directly with leading US-based health systems, hospitals, and large physician groups, enabling it to build direct relationships and optimise revenue cycle operations across patient access, coding, billing, and collections. This helps healthcare providers maximise revenue realisation, reduce administrative costs, and focus on delivering clinical care.\r\n\r\nAs of March 2026, AGS Health served 82 health systems and hospital customers, including 11 of the top 20 hospitals in the US. Its client base includes leading healthcare providers such as Baylor Scott &amp;amp; White Health, Barton Health, Curana Health, Duke Health, National Seating &amp;amp; Mobility, Renown Health, St. Joseph's Health, ApolloMD, and Sharp HealthCare.\r\n\r\nOn the financial front, AGS Health, which competes with peer Inventurus Knowledge Solutions, reported a consolidated profit of Rs 206.9 crore and revenue of Rs 2,041.4 crore for the financial year ended March 2026.\r\n\r\nOn a standalone basis, the company's profit rose 23.6 percent to Rs 142.9 crore in FY25 from Rs 115.6 crore in FY24, while revenue increased 20.8 percent to Rs 1,194.9 crore from Rs 989 crore during the same period.\r\n\r\nICICI Securities, Jefferies India, JM Financial, J.P. Morgan India, and Nomura Financial Advisory and Securities (India) have been appointed as the merchant bankers to manage the AGS Health IPO.",
