          "1": {
            "id": "13998395",
            "headline": "Dhoot Transmission raises Rs 918 crore from anchor investors ahead of August 10 IPO",
            "heading": "Dhoot Transmission raises Rs 918 crore from anchor investors ahead of August 10 IPO",
            "intro": "Dhoot Transmission IPO | The company tapped capital markets to raise up to Rs 3,067-crore via initial public offering at the upper end of price band of Rs 829-871 per share.",
            "body": "Dhoot Transmission, the Maharashtra-based manufacturer of wiring harnesses and electrical distribution systems for automotive and non-automotive applications, has raised Rs 918.3 crore from anchor investors ahead of its initial public offering (IPO), which opens for public subscription on August 10.\r\n\r\nThe company is looking to raise up to Rs 3,067 crore through the IPO at the upper end of the price band of Rs 829-871 per share. The public issue comprises a fresh issue of Rs 1,400 crore and an offer for sale (OFS) of up to 1.91 crore shares by promoter entities BC Asia Investments XV, owned by Bain Capital, and Mangalam Capital. The issue will close on August 12.\r\n\r\nAccording to the company's exchange filing on August 7, Dhoot Transmission allotted 1.05 crore equity shares to 72 anchor investors at Rs 871 per share, raising Rs 918.3 crore.\r\n\r\nGlobal investors including BlackRock, Abu Dhabi Investment Authority (ADIA), Amundi and Chartered Finance &amp;amp; Leasing participated in the anchor book.\r\n\r\nOf the total allocation, 64.59 lakh equity shares were allotted to 12 domestic mutual funds through 46 schemes, including SBI Mutual Fund, ICICI Prudential AMC, HDFC Mutual Fund, Axis Mutual Fund, Mirae Asset, Nippon India Mutual Fund, Franklin Templeton, Tata Mutual Fund, Invesco Mutual Fund, HSBC Mutual Fund, PGIM India Mutual Fund and Sundaram Mutual Fund.\r\n\r\nClick Here To Read All IPO News\r\nLife insurers including SBI Life Insurance, HDFC Life Insurance, ICICI Prudential Life Insurance, Axis Max Life Insurance and Bajaj Allianz Life Insurance also participated in the anchor book, acquiring 9.21 lakh shares worth Rs 80.3 crore.\r\n\r\nAccording to market observers, Dhoot Transmission's shares were trading at a grey market premium (GMP) of around 29 percent ahead of the IPO.\r\n\r\nThe company designs and manufactures wiring harnesses and operates 22 manufacturing facilities, three engineering and design support centres and seven warehouses across India and international markets. The wiring harness business contributed 77 percent of its revenue in FY26.\r\n\r\nDhoot Transmission plans to utilise Rs 766.5 crore from the fresh issue proceeds for debt repayment. Another Rs 150 crore will be used to set up a new wiring harness manufacturing facility, while the remaining funds will be deployed for inorganic growth through acquisitions and general corporate purposes.\r\n\r\nFor FY26, the company reported a 12.1 percent year-on-year increase in profit to Rs 396.8 crore, while revenue grew 31.4 percent to Rs 4,525 crore.\r\n\r\nThe book-running lead managers to the issue are Axis Capital, Jefferies India, Kotak Mahindra Capital Company, Nomura Financial Advisory and Securities (India), SBI Capital Markets and 360 ONE WAM.",
            "posturl": "news/business/ipo/dhoot-transmission-raises-rs-918-crore-from-anchor-investors-ahead-of-august-10-ipo-13998395.html",
