          "2": {
            "id": "13998375",
            "headline": "Molbio Diagnostics raises Rs 281 crore from anchor investors ahead of Rs 940 crore IPO",
            "heading": "Molbio Diagnostics raises Rs 281 crore from anchor investors ahead of Rs 940 crore IPO",
            "intro": "Molbio Diagnostics IPO | The Temasek and Motilal Oswal Group-backed company is set to open its Rs 940-crore public issue for the public on August 10.",
            "body": "Molbio Diagnostics, the Goa-based point-of-care molecular diagnostics company, has raised Rs 281.5 crore from anchor investors ahead of its initial public offering (IPO), which opens for public subscription on August 10.\r\n\r\nThe Temasek and Motilal Oswal Group-backed company plans to raise Rs 940 crore through the IPO, comprising a fresh issue of Rs 200 crore and an offer for sale (OFS) of 91.66 lakh shares worth Rs 739.7 crore by existing shareholders. The issue will close on August 12.\r\n\r\nThe price band for the IPO has been fixed at Rs 768-807 per share.\r\n\r\nAccording to the company's exchange filing dated August 7, Molbio Diagnostics allotted 34.87 lakh equity shares to 33 anchor investors, raising Rs 281.5 crore.\r\n\r\nAmong global investors, Goldman Sachs invested Rs 30 crore, while the International Finance Corporation (IFC) and BlackRock Global Funds invested Rs 20 crore each through the anchor book.\r\n\r\n&quot;Out of the total allocation of 34.87 lakh equity shares to anchor investors, 23.54 lakh shares were allotted to nine domestic mutual funds through 19 schemes,&quot; the company said.\r\n\r\nThe participating mutual funds included HDFC Mutual Fund, Kotak Mahindra AMC, ICICI Prudential AMC, Nippon India Mutual Fund, Mirae Asset, WhiteOak Capital, Motilal Oswal AMC, Tata Mutual Fund, and Edelweiss Mutual Fund.\r\n\r\nClick Here To Read All IPO News\r\n\r\nThe company also allotted 2.65 lakh shares worth Rs 21.44 crore to 10 life insurance companies.\r\n\r\nAccording to market observers, Molbio Diagnostics' shares were commanding a grey market premium (GMP) of over 20 percent ahead of the IPO.\r\n\r\nMolbio Diagnostics has developed the Truenat platform, which is patented in more than 100 countries for diagnosing infectious and non-communicable diseases. The company currently offers molecular diagnostic tests for 30 diseases through 43 assays, including tuberculosis, COVID-19, Hepatitis B and C, HIV and Human Papillomavirus (HPV).\r\n\r\nThe company plans to utilise Rs 105.5 crore from the fresh issue proceeds to establish a research and development facility and a Centre of Excellence, to be operated by its subsidiary Bigtec, along with office space for the company, its subsidiaries and associate entities.\r\n\r\nAnother Rs 72.2 crore will be used to purchase plant, machinery and equipment for its manufacturing units in Goa and Visakhapatnam, while the remaining proceeds will be used for general corporate purposes.\r\n\r\nKotak Mahindra Capital Company, IIFL Capital Services, Jefferies India and Motilal Oswal Investment Advisors are the book-running lead managers to the issue.",
